  },
  {
   "text": "After hours CP rate",
   "where": "build/founder-mode/what-why/sources/design-2026-10-27-artifact/files/DialogBefore.dc.html:57",
   "in_a_case": false,
   "library": false,
   "on_a_board": true,
   "class": ""
  },
  {
   "text": "What a writer sees today",
   "where": "build/founder-mode/what-why/sources/design-2026-10-27-artifact/files/DialogBefore.dc.html:80",
   "in_a_case": false,
   "library": false,
   "on_a_board": true,
   "class": ""
  },
  {
   "text": "Each field is named by the question it asks. Nothing on screen says what the values are called, so whatever is typed is read back elsewhere as the answer to a question, including in a shop's accounting records.",
   "where": "build/founder-mode/what-why/sources/design-2026-10-27-artifact/files/DialogBefore.dc.html:81",
   "in_a_case": false,
   "library": false,
   "on_a_board": true,
   "class": ""
  },
  {
   "text": "Extreme cases",
   "where": "build/founder-mode/what-why/sources/design-2026-10-27-artifact/files/EdgeCases.dc.html:25",
   "in_a_case": false,
   "library": false,
   "on_a_board": true,
   "class": ""
  },
  {
   "text": "What the joined line reads when the inputs are awkward. Three segments, one separator, and a separator only ever appears between two things that are both present.",
   "where": "build/founder-mode/what-why/sources/design-2026-10-27-artifact/files/EdgeCases.dc.html:26",
   "in_a_case": false,
   "library": false,
   "on_a_board": true,
   "class": ""
  },
  {
   "text": "S3-R3 · no description",
   "where": "build/founder-mode/what-why/sources/design-2026-10-27-artifact/files/EdgeCases.dc.html:32",
   "in_a_case": false,
   "library": false,
   "on_a_board": true,
   "class": ""
  },
  {
   "text": "One separator, not two. The empty description leaves no gap and no double hyphen behind it.",
   "where": "build/founder-mode/what-why/sources/design-2026-10-27-artifact/files/EdgeCases.dc.html:41",
   "in_a_case": false,
   "library": false,
   "on_a_board": true,
   "class": ""
  },
  {
   "text": "S3-R9 · the title already contains a hyphen",
   "where": "build/founder-mode/what-why/sources/design-2026-10-27-artifact/files/EdgeCases.dc.html:45",
   "in_a_case": false,
   "library": false,
   "on_a_board": true,
   "class": ""
  },
  {
   "text": "Replace tie rod - passenger side",
   "where": "build/founder-mode/what-why/sources/design-2026-10-27-artifact/files/EdgeCases.dc.html:47",
   "in_a_case": false,
   "library": false,
   "on_a_board": true,
   "class": ""
  },
  {
   "text": "Torqued to 74 ft-lb, alignment set",
   "where": "build/founder-mode/what-why/sources/design-2026-10-27-artifact/files/EdgeCases.dc.html:49",
   "in_a_case": false,
   "library": false,
   "on_a_board": true,
   "class": ""
  },
  {
   "text": "Replace tie rod - passenger side - excessive play - customer waiting - Torqued to 74 ft-lb, alignment set",
   "where": "build/founder-mode/what-why/sources/design-2026-10-27-artifact/files/EdgeCases.dc.html:53",
   "in_a_case": false,
   "library": false,
   "on_a_board": true,
   "class": ""
  },
  {
   "text": "Carried as written. Nothing is escaped or quoted, so a reader cannot tell our separator from theirs. This is the cost of the choice and it is accepted deliberately: the alternative is printing a field name to mark the join, which is the thing two customers asked us to stop doing.",
   "where": "build/founder-mode/what-why/sources/design-2026-10-27-artifact/files/EdgeCases.dc.html:54",
   "in_a_case": false,
   "library": false,
   "on_a_board": true,
   "class": ""
  },
  {
   "text": "The four flavours of tech story that reach the books",
   "where": "build/founder-mode/what-why/sources/design-2026-10-27-artifact/files/EdgeCases.dc.html:58",
   "in_a_case": false,
   "library": false,
   "on_a_board": true,
   "class": ""
  },
  {
   "text": "Written at the completion gate · Require Tech Story ON",
   "where": "build/founder-mode/what-why/sources/design-2026-10-27-artifact/files/EdgeCases.dc.html:61",
   "in_a_case": false,
   "library": false,
   "on_a_board": true,
   "class": ""
  },
  {
   "text": "Require Tech Story OFF · the shop never wrote one",
   "where": "build/founder-mode/what-why/sources/design-2026-10-27-artifact/files/EdgeCases.dc.html:65",
   "in_a_case": false,
   "library": false,
   "on_a_board": true,
   "class": ""
  },
  {
   "text": "The “Tech story missing.” placeholder · suppressed, as both invoice views suppress it",
   "where": "build/founder-mode/what-why/sources/design-2026-10-27-artifact/files/EdgeCases.dc.html:69",
   "in_a_case": false,
   "library": false,
   "on_a_board": true,
   "class": ""
  },
  {
   "text": "Imported from a previous system · may be empty",
   "where": "build/founder-mode/what-why/sources/design-2026-10-27-artifact/files/EdgeCases.dc.html:73",
   "in_a_case": false,
   "library": false,
   "on_a_board": true,
   "class": ""
  },
  {
   "text": "Three of these four end after the description, and none of them leaves a trailing hyphen. The placeholder case is the one worth arguing about: “Tech story missing.” is written by the line dialog when nothing was typed, and both invoice views already refuse to print it to a customer. The books should not be the one place it shows up.",
   "where": "build/founder-mode/what-why/sources/design-2026-10-27-artifact/files/EdgeCases.dc.html:77",
   "in_a_case": false,
   "library": false,
   "on_a_board": true,
   "class": ""
  },
  {
   "text": "excessive play; also checked the drag link",
   "where": "build/founder-mode/what-why/sources/design-2026-10-27-artifact/files/EdgeCases.dc.html:84",
   "in_a_case": false,
   "library": false,
   "on_a_board": true,
   "class": ""
  },
  {
   "text": "Drag link within spec",
   "where": "build/founder-mode/what-why/sources/design-2026-10-27-artifact/files/EdgeCases.dc.html:85",
   "in_a_case": false,
   "library": false,
   "on_a_board": true,
   "class": ""
  },
  {
   "text": "Replace tie rod - excessive play; also checked the drag link - Drag link within spec",
   "where": "build/founder-mode/what-why/sources/design-2026-10-27-artifact/files/EdgeCases.dc.html:89",
   "in_a_case": false,
   "library": false,
   "on_a_board": true,
   "class": ""
  },
  {
   "text": "This was an open question while the semicolon was the separator: a typed one was indistinguishable from a new segment, and anything splitting on it broke. With the semicolon gone, a typed semicolon is ordinary punctuation and carries through untouched. The question does not need answering any more.",
   "where": "build/founder-mode/what-why/sources/design-2026-10-27-artifact/files/EdgeCases.dc.html:90",
   "in_a_case": false,
   "library": false,
   "on_a_board": true,
   "class": ""
  },
  {
   "text": "Edit Line · after · S1-R1, S1-R2, S1-R4",
   "where": "build/founder-mode/what-why/sources/design-2026-10-27-artifact/files/EditAfter.dc.html:25",
   "in_a_case": false,
   "library": false,
   "on_a_board": true,
   "class": ""
  },
  {
   "text": "HD Fleet Rate",
   "where": "build/founder-mode/what-why/sources/design-2026-10-27-artifact/files/EditAfter.dc.html:66",
   "in_a_case": false,
   "library": false,
   "on_a_board": true,
   "class": ""
  },
  {
   "text": "Two labels, nothing else",
   "where": "build/founder-mode/what-why/sources/design-2026-10-27-artifact/files/EditAfter.dc.html:93",
   "in_a_case": false,
   "library": false,
   "on_a_board": true,
   "class": ""
  },
  {
   "text": "The floating labels now read",
   "where": "build/founder-mode/what-why/sources/design-2026-10-27-artifact/files/EditAfter.dc.html:94",
   "in_a_case": false,
   "library": false,
   "on_a_board": true,
   "class": ""
  },
  {
   "text": ", so a filled field is named rather than interrogated. The empty Description still prompts with “Why are you doing it?” in sentence case.",
   "where": "build/founder-mode/what-why/sources/design-2026-10-27-artifact/files/EditAfter.dc.html:94",
   "in_a_case": false,
   "library": false,
   "on_a_board": true,
   "class": ""
  },
  {
   "text": "Status, Technicians, the labor row, the ShopCoach link, Delete and Save & Close are all untouched. Edit mode has no canned-line picker, so the state-dependent label S1-R4 removes was a New Line problem only.",
   "where": "build/founder-mode/what-why/sources/design-2026-10-27-artifact/files/EditAfter.dc.html:95",
   "in_a_case": false,
   "library": false,
   "on_a_board": true,
   "class": ""
  },
  {
   "text": "Edit Line · before",
   "where": "build/founder-mode/what-why/sources/design-2026-10-27-artifact/files/EditBefore.dc.html:25",
   "in_a_case": false,
   "library": false,
   "on_a_board": true,
   "class": ""
  },
  {
   "text": "The question is worst here",
   "where": "build/founder-mode/what-why/sources/design-2026-10-27-artifact/files/EditBefore.dc.html:92",
   "in_a_case": false,
   "library": false,
   "on_a_board": true,
   "class": ""
  },
  {
   "text": "With a value in the field, the label floats up and sits directly above the words it supposedly names. “Replace - Brake pot” reads as the answer to “What Are You Doing?” rather than as the name of the job, which is exactly how it then arrives in the shop's books.",
   "where": "build/founder-mode/what-why/sources/design-2026-10-27-artifact/files/EditBefore.dc.html:93",
   "in_a_case": false,
   "library": false,
   "on_a_board": true,
   "class": ""
  },
  {
   "text": "After · S1-R1 to S1-R5",
   "where": "build/founder-mode/what-why/sources/design-2026-10-27-artifact/files/Main.dc.html:23",
   "in_a_case": false,
   "library": false,
   "on_a_board": true,
   "class": ""
  },
  {
   "text": "The only two things that change",
   "where": "build/founder-mode/what-why/sources/design-2026-10-27-artifact/files/Main.dc.html:84",
   "in_a_case": false,
   "library": false,
   "on_a_board": true,
   "class": ""
  },
  {
   "text": "The field is now named",
   "where": "build/founder-mode/what-why/sources/design-2026-10-27-artifact/files/Main.dc.html:85",
   "in_a_case": false,
   "library": false,
   "on_a_board": true,
   "class": ""
  },
  {
   "text": "and the question moves inside it as the prompt, in sentence case: “What are you doing?”. Same for",
   "where": "build/founder-mode/what-why/sources/design-2026-10-27-artifact/files/Main.dc.html:85",
   "in_a_case": false,
   "library": false,
   "on_a_board": true,
   "class": ""
  },
  {
   "text": "Require Tech Story OFF, none written",
   "where": "build/founder-mode/what-why/sources/design-2026-10-27-artifact/files/QuickBooks.dc.html:103",
   "in_a_case": false,
   "library": false,
   "on_a_board": true,
   "class": ""
  },
  {
   "text": "No trailing hyphen and no trailing space. A separator appears only when there is something on both sides of it, which is the same rule the description already follows.",
   "where": "build/founder-mode/what-why/sources/design-2026-10-27-artifact/files/QuickBooks.dc.html:107",
   "in_a_case": false,
   "library": false,
   "on_a_board": true,
   "class": ""
  },
  {
   "text": "The line a bookkeeper reads",
   "where": "build/founder-mode/what-why/sources/design-2026-10-27-artifact/files/QuickBooks.dc.html:23",
   "in_a_case": false,
   "library": false,
   "on_a_board": true,
   "class": ""
  },
  {
   "text": "One builder feeds both routes: the live QuickBooks sync and the downloadable Customer Invoice report · S3-R1 to S3-R4",
   "where": "build/founder-mode/what-why/sources/design-2026-10-27-artifact/files/QuickBooks.dc.html:24",
   "in_a_case": false,
   "library": false,
   "on_a_board": true,
   "class": ""
  },
  {
   "text": "What are you doing?: Front brake pads;Why are you doing it?: Customer reports grinding;Tech Story: Pads at 2mm, rotors turned, bed-in road test",
   "where": "build/founder-mode/what-why/sources/design-2026-10-27-artifact/files/QuickBooks.dc.html:40",
   "in_a_case": false,
   "library": false,
   "on_a_board": true,
   "class": ""
  },
  {
   "text": "Front brake pads - Customer reports grinding - Pads at 2mm, rotors turned, bed-in road test",
   "where": "build/founder-mode/what-why/sources/design-2026-10-27-artifact/files/QuickBooks.dc.html:61",
   "in_a_case": false,
   "library": false,
   "on_a_board": true,
   "class": ""
  },
  {
   "text": "Title, description, then the technician's narrative, each separated by a spaced hyphen. No semicolons and no field names of ours anywhere in the field.",
   "where": "build/founder-mode/what-why/sources/design-2026-10-27-artifact/files/QuickBooks.dc.html:66",
   "in_a_case": false,
   "library": false,
   "on_a_board": true,
   "class": ""
  },
  {
   "text": "Why the narrative carries no label",
   "where": "build/founder-mode/what-why/sources/design-2026-10-27-artifact/files/QuickBooks.dc.html:70",
   "in_a_case": false,
   "library": false,
   "on_a_board": true,
   "class": ""
  },
  {
   "text": "Because the two invoice views disagree about the label and agree about everything else. Legacy prints the narrative as a plain paragraph under the description with no label at all. Modern prints it under a “Scope of work” heading. Both print the title and the description with no labels, both put the narrative last, and both drop it entirely when it is empty or reads “Tech story missing.” Printing no label is the only choice that matches what a customer sees in either view.",
   "where": "build/founder-mode/what-why/sources/design-2026-10-27-artifact/files/QuickBooks.dc.html:71",
   "in_a_case": false,
   "library": false,
   "on_a_board": true,
   "class": ""
  },
  {
   "text": "Legacy invoice",
   "where": "build/founder-mode/what-why/sources/design-2026-10-27-artifact/files/QuickBooks.dc.html:74",
   "in_a_case": false,
   "library": false,
   "on_a_board": true,
   "class": ""
  },
  {
   "text": "Modern invoice",
   "where": "build/founder-mode/what-why/sources/design-2026-10-27-artifact/files/QuickBooks.dc.html:82",
   "in_a_case": false,
   "library": false,
   "on_a_board": true,
   "class": ""
  },
  {
   "text": "Scope of work",
   "where": "build/founder-mode/what-why/sources/design-2026-10-27-artifact/files/QuickBooks.dc.html:86",
   "in_a_case": false,
   "library": false,
   "on_a_board": true,
   "class": ""
  },
  {
   "text": "Drawn from the templates rather than from memory: legacy at batch-invoice.html.twig lines 679 to 690, modern at invoice.html.twig lines 1549 to 1557.",
   "where": "build/founder-mode/what-why/sources/design-2026-10-27-artifact/files/QuickBooks.dc.html:91",
   "in_a_case": false,
   "library": false,
   "on_a_board": true,
   "class": ""
  },
  {
   "text": "Whether a line has a narrative at all is a shop setting",
   "where": "build/founder-mode/what-why/sources/design-2026-10-27-artifact/files/QuickBooks.dc.html:95",
   "in_a_case": false,
   "library": false,
   "on_a_board": true,
   "class": ""
  },
  {
   "text": ": “Tech story will be a required field before a line can be completed on a work order.” With it on, the completion flow stops on a gate and refuses an empty value, so every invoiced line carries one and the two rows above are what a bookkeeper sees. With it off, a line is completed and invoiced with nothing there, and the line has to end cleanly after the description.",
   "where": "build/founder-mode/what-why/sources/design-2026-10-27-artifact/files/QuickBooks.dc.html:96",
   "in_a_case": false,
   "library": false,
   "on_a_board": true,
   "class": ""
  },
  {
   "text": "Require Tech Story ON",
   "where": "build/founder-mode/what-why/sources/design-2026-10-27-artifact/files/QuickBooks.dc.html:99",
   "in_a_case": false,
   "library": false,
   "on_a_board": true,
   "class": ""
  },
  {
   "text": "The long end of the scale",
   "where": "build/founder-mode/what-why/sources/design-2026-10-27-artifact/files/Truncation.dc.html:23",
   "in_a_case": false,
   "library": false,
   "on_a_board": true,
   "class": ""
  },
  {
   "text": "ShopView allows 255 characters of title and 65,535 of description. Both routes into QuickBooks, the live sync and the downloaded report, cut at 4,000 bytes. S3-R7 decides what survives.",
   "where": "build/founder-mode/what-why/sources/design-2026-10-27-artifact/files/Truncation.dc.html:24",
   "in_a_case": false,
   "library": false,
   "on_a_board": true,
   "class": ""
  },
  {
   "text": "S3-R7 · the cut lands in the description, never the title",
   "where": "build/founder-mode/what-why/sources/design-2026-10-27-artifact/files/Truncation.dc.html:28",
   "in_a_case": false,
   "library": false,
   "on_a_board": true,
   "class": ""
  },
  {
   "text": "Title · always survives",
   "where": "build/founder-mode/what-why/sources/design-2026-10-27-artifact/files/Truncation.dc.html:31",
   "in_a_case": false,
   "library": false,
   "on_a_board": true,
   "class": ""
  },
  {
   "text": "Description · clipped at the limit",
   "where": "build/founder-mode/what-why/sources/design-2026-10-27-artifact/files/Truncation.dc.html:35",
   "in_a_case": false,
   "library": false,
   "on_a_board": true,
   "class": ""
  },
  {
   "text": "excessive play in the steering, both outer ends replaced, alignment checked and set to spec, road tested twelve miles, no pull, no vibration at speed, customer advised to return in 500 miles for a re-tor",
   "where": "build/founder-mode/what-why/sources/design-2026-10-27-artifact/files/Truncation.dc.html:36",
   "in_a_case": false,
   "library": false,
   "on_a_board": true,
   "class": ""
  },
  {
   "text": "que and the remaining 1,400 characters",
   "where": "build/founder-mode/what-why/sources/design-2026-10-27-artifact/files/Truncation.dc.html:40",
   "in_a_case": false,
   "library": false,
   "on_a_board": true,
   "class": ""
  },
  {
   "text": "The title leads the joined string, so whatever survives always begins with it. A shop that writes essays loses the tail of the essay, never the name of the job.",
   "where": "build/founder-mode/what-why/sources/design-2026-10-27-artifact/files/Truncation.dc.html:43",
   "in_a_case": false,
   "library": false,
   "on_a_board": true,
   "class": ""
  },
  {
   "text": "The order matters more now that the narrative is the third segment. It is the longest of the three by a wide margin, and it sits last, so it is what gets clipped. Title, then description, then narrative is also the order both invoice views print them in, so a cut takes the least important thing first in every case.",
   "where": "build/founder-mode/what-why/sources/design-2026-10-27-artifact/files/Truncation.dc.html:44",
   "in_a_case": false,
   "library": false,
   "on_a_board": true,
   "class": ""
  },
  {
   "text": "Answered 2026-09-16 · now S3-R7 and S3-R7a",
   "where": "build/founder-mode/what-why/sources/design-2026-10-27-artifact/files/Truncation.dc.html:48",
   "in_a_case": false,
   "library": false,
   "on_a_board": true,
   "class": ""
  },
  {
   "text": "Shorten until it fits, and never split a character",
   "where": "build/founder-mode/what-why/sources/design-2026-10-27-artifact/files/Truncation.dc.html:49",
   "in_a_case": false,
   "library": false,
   "on_a_board": true,
   "class": ""
  },
  {
   "text": "What the build does today",
   "where": "build/founder-mode/what-why/sources/design-2026-10-27-artifact/files/Truncation.dc.html:52",
   "in_a_case": false,
   "library": false,
   "on_a_board": true,
   "class": ""
  },
  {
   "text": "…biellette de direction côté passa",
   "where": "build/founder-mode/what-why/sources/design-2026-10-27-artifact/files/Truncation.dc.html:53",
   "in_a_case": false,
   "library": false,
   "on_a_board": true,
   "class": ""
  },
  {
   "text": "[half of é]",
   "where": "build/founder-mode/what-why/sources/design-2026-10-27-artifact/files/Truncation.dc.html:53",
   "in_a_case": false,
   "library": false,
   "on_a_board": true,
   "class": ""
